# Feedback

The publishing feedback component collects a response about the page. It is separate from contacting an organisation or reporting an urgent problem. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/components/feedback/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

For civica.uk documentation, offer a clear route to report a documentation problem or suggest an improvement. Explain the destination and that a public issue may be visible to others. In the HA interface, use the existing support path for the affected integration or component.

## Structure and behaviour

If a service collects feedback, label each field and confirm receipt only after a real successful response. Keep entered text available on failure. Make an email address optional unless the service genuinely needs it. Explain the purpose of any contact details before collection.

## Home Assistant boundary

The examples acknowledge activity locally and do not send feedback. No analytics, GOV.UK survey endpoint, notification service or email collection is installed by this reference. A successful local demonstration must never be described as a submitted report.

